{
  "meta": {
    "site": "https://github.com/zengfr/n8n-workflow-all-templates",
    "tokenfree": "https://tokenyep.com/",
    "name": "Create platform-specific social posts from blog RSS with PostWire",
    "wechat": "youandme10086",
    "id": 18716,
    "update_time": "2026-09-27"
  },
  "name": "Blog RSS to native social posts, logged in Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "Note: overview",
      "name": "Note: overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        -340
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Every new blog post, rewritten for each network and logged in a Sheet\n\nYour RSS feed is already the list of things worth talking about. This watches it, and when something\nnew appears it writes a **different** post for each network, queues them, and records what went out\nin a Google Sheet so you have a content log without keeping one by hand.\n\n@[youtube](Tcak2lt2k3s)\n\n### What it does, in order\n1. Checks your feed hourly (n8n remembers what it has seen, so nothing is picked up twice).\n2. Drops anything older than two days — the first run of an RSS trigger otherwise returns the archive.\n3. Pulls out the title, link, summary and image.\n4. Removes Instagram from the target list when the article has no image, instead of failing everything.\n5. Writes one caption per network with PostWire, then queues them 30 minutes out.\n6. **Appends a row to Google Sheets** with the date, title, link and which networks it went to.\n7. **Emails you** if the queue call fails, so a broken feed does not fail silently for a week.\n\n### What you need\n- A **PostWire** account (free tier is enough) — https://postwire.io — API key from *API & MCP*.\n- A **Google Sheet** with the columns: `date`, `title`, `link`, `networks`, `status`.\n- Gmail connected in n8n, if you want the failure alert.\n\n### Setup\n1. Header Auth credential: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer pw_live_...`\n2. Put your feed URL in the RSS trigger and your Sheet ID in the two Sheets nodes.\n3. Edit the `platforms` list to the networks you actually connected in PostWire.\n4. Run once by hand and check the Sheet filled in."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Note: the feed",
      "name": "Note: the feed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        -340
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "### 1. Watch the feed\n\nHourly. n8n remembers what it has already seen, so an article is only ever picked up once."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Note: skip the backlog",
      "name": "Note: skip the backlog",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        460,
        -340
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "### 2. Only genuinely new items\n\nThe first run of an RSS trigger can return the whole archive. Anything older than two days is dropped, so you don't wake up to forty queued posts."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Note: media decides",
      "name": "Note: media decides",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        920,
        -340
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "### 3. The image decides the networks\n\nInstagram needs a picture. Without one it is dropped from the list and the rest still go out — one missing asset should not block the whole post."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Note: per-network captions",
      "name": "Note: per-network captions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1840,
        -340
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "### 4. One draft, many captions\n\n`/api/generate` returns a caption per network, written to that network's own limits and tone."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Note: the log",
      "name": "Note: the log",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3760,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "### 5. Queue it, then log it\n\nScheduled 30 minutes out so there is time to edit. The Sheet row is your content log — what went out, when, and where — without keeping one by hand."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Note: failures are loud",
      "name": "Note: failures are loud",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3180,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "### 6. A failure that tells you\n\nIf the queue call fails, the false branch emails you with the article and the reason. A feed that silently stops posting is worse than one that breaks noisily."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "rss",
      "name": "Watch the feed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.rssFeedReadTrigger",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "feedUrl": "https://example.com/blog/rss.xml",
        "options": {},
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyHour"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fresh",
      "name": "Only the last 2 days",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "position": [
        460,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "fresh",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ new Date($json.isoDate || $json.pubDate).getTime() > Date.now() - 2 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000 }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "shape",
      "name": "Pick the networks",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        920,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "title",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.title }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "link",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.link }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a3",
              "name": "summary",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ ($json.contentSnippet || $json.content || '').replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').trim().slice(0, 600) }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a4",
              "name": "photo_url",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.enclosure?.url || ($json.content || '').match(/<img[^>]+src=[\"']([^\"']+)/)?.[1] || '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a5",
              "name": "platforms",
              "type": "array",
              "value": "={{ ['linkedin', 'x', 'bluesky', 'mastodon', 'instagram'] }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "media",
      "name": "Drop IG if no image",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        1380,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "b1",
              "name": "platforms",
              "type": "array",
              "value": "={{ $json.photo_url ? $json.platforms : $json.platforms.filter(p => p !== 'instagram') }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "b2",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ 'New article: ' + $json.title + '\\n\\n' + $json.summary + '\\n\\nLink: ' + $json.link }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": true
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "gen",
      "name": "Caption per network",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        1840,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://postwire.io/api/generate",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {},
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ prompt: $json.prompt, platforms: $json.platforms, media_url: $json.photo_url || undefined }) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "sched",
      "name": "Queue in 30 min",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        2300,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://postwire.io/api/schedule",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": true,
              "fullResponse": true
            }
          }
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ run_at: new Date(Date.now() + 30 * 60 * 1000).toISOString(), platforms: $('Drop IG if no image').item.json.platforms, label: $('Pick the networks').item.json.title.slice(0, 60), photo_url: $('Pick the networks').item.json.photo_url || undefined, per_platform: $json.drafts }) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "okcheck",
      "name": "Did it queue?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        2760,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "ok",
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "lt"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.statusCode }}",
              "rightValue": 300
            }
          ]
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "log",
      "name": "Log to Sheet",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        3220,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {
            "date": "={{ $now.format('yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm') }}",
            "link": "={{ $('Pick the networks').item.json.link }}",
            "title": "={{ $('Pick the networks').item.json.title }}",
            "status": "queued",
            "networks": "={{ $('Drop IG if no image').item.json.platforms.join(', ') }}"
          },
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow"
        },
        "options": {},
        "operation": "append",
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "Sheet1"
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "YOUR_SHEET_ID"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.5
    },
    {
      "id": "alert",
      "name": "Email the failure",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "position": [
        3220,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "you@example.com",
        "message": "=The article was not queued.\\n\\nTitle: {{ $('Pick the networks').item.json.title }}\\nLink: {{ $('Pick the networks').item.json.link }}\\nNetworks: {{ $('Drop IG if no image').item.json.platforms.join(', ') }}\\n\\nWhat PostWire said:\\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.body) }}",
        "options": {},
        "subject": "=PostWire could not queue: {{ $('Pick the networks').item.json.title }}",
        "emailType": "text"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.1
    }
  ],
